Package: jkit
Version: [[version]]
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: [[deb.arch]]
Maintainer: [[package.maintainer]]
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), zlib1g
Homepage: https://jkit-project.dev
Description: installs and switches JDKs, Maven, Gradle and sbt
 jkit is a single native command-line tool that installs and switches
 JDKs from many vendors (Temurin, Corretto, Zulu, Liberica, GraalVM and
 others), Maven, Gradle and sbt. It needs no JDK to run.
 .
 Enable switching in the current shell with: eval "$(jkit hook bash)"
